  "result": "I added `compareVersions(a, b)` in `src/core/semver.ts` and committed it as `3416add`. The new tests, `tsc`, `biome check` and `scripts/boundaries.ts` all pass. I didn't run the full `npm test` suite.\n\n- **Behavior:** it compares each dotted part as a number, so `1.10.0` sorts above `1.9.0`. Missing trailing parts count as 0, so `1.2` equals `1.2.0`. It returns -1, 0 or 1. Input that isn't dotted digits, such as `1.x`, throws an `Invalid version` error.\n- **Tests:** `test/core/semver.test.ts` covers numeric-versus-lexical ordering, missing parts and the throw on bad input.\n- **Reuse:** I found nothing in `src/` that compares versions or would make this shorter, so it uses no existing helpers.",
